# 中频词汇 List09
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List09核心词汇

{{ignorance}}{/ˈɪɡnərəns/}{无知；愚昧}{Ignorance of the law is no excuse for breaking it.}}
{{illustrate}}{/ˈɪləstreɪt/}{说明；插图}{The chart illustrates the growth trend over the past decade.}}
{{immense}}{/ɪˈmens/}{巨大的；无限的}{The project requires an immense amount of coordination.}}
{{immune}}{/ɪˈmjuːn/}{免疫的；豁免的}{The vaccine helps the body build immunity to the virus.}}
{{impact}}{/ˈɪmpækt/}{影响；冲击}{The policy had a positive impact on the local economy.}}
{{implement}}{/ˈɪmplɪment/}{实施；执行}{The new system will be implemented next quarter.}}
{{implication}}{/ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn/}{含义；暗示}{The ruling has far-reaching implications for the industry.}}
{{implicit}}{/ɪmˈplɪsɪt/}{含蓄的；隐含的}{There was an implicit understanding between the partners.}}
{{impose}}{/ɪmˈpəʊz/}{施加；强加}{The government imposed a curfew during the emergency.}}
{{incentive}}{/ɪnˈsentɪv/}{激励；动机}{Tax incentives encourage businesses to invest in research.}}
{{inclined}}{/ɪnˈklaɪnd/}{倾向于；有意向的}{She is inclined to agree with the proposal.}}
{{incorporate}}{/ɪnˈkɔːpəreɪt/}{包含；合并}{The new design incorporates feedback from users.}}
{{incredible}}{/ɪnˈkredəbl/}{难以置信的；惊人的}{The athlete showed incredible determination.}}
{{indication}}{/ˌɪndɪˈkeɪʃn/}{表明；指示}{There is no indication that the trend will reverse.}}
{{indifferent}}{/ɪnˈdɪfərənt/}{冷漠的；不关心的}{He seemed indifferent to the outcome of the vote.}}
{{indispensable}}{/ˌɪndɪˈspensəbl/}{不可或缺的}{Technology has become indispensable in modern education.}}
{{induce}}{/ɪnˈdjuːs/}{诱导；引起}{The drug can induce drowsiness in some patients.}}
{{infer}}{/ɪnˈfɜːr/}{推断；推论}{We can infer from the data that the trend is upward.}}
{{inflate}}{/ɪnˈfleɪt/}{膨胀；夸大}{The figures were inflated to attract investors.}}
{{inherent}}{/ɪnˈhɪərənt/}{固有的；内在的}{There are inherent risks in any investment.}}
{{inhabit}}{/ɪnˈhæbɪt/}{居住；栖息}{The island is inhabited by a small fishing community.}}
{{inhibit}}{/ɪnˈhɪbɪt/}{抑制；阻碍}{Fear of failure can inhibit creativity.}}
{{initiative}}{/ɪˈnɪʃətɪv/}{倡议；主动性}{The government launched a new green energy initiative.}}
{{injure}}{/ˈɪndʒər/}{伤害；损伤}{Several workers were injured in the accident.}}
{{innocent}}{/ˈɪnəsnt/}{无辜的；天真的}{The jury declared the defendant innocent.}}
{{innovation}}{/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn/}{创新；革新}{Innovation is the key driver of long-term economic growth.}}
{{input}}{/ˈɪnpʊt/}{投入；输入}{We value input from all stakeholders.}}
{{insist}}{/ɪnˈsɪst/}{坚持；坚决要求}{She insisted on paying for the dinner.}}
{{inspect}}{/ɪnˈspekt/}{检查；视察}{Health inspectors regularly inspect restaurants.}}
{{inspire}}{/ɪnˈspaɪər/}{激励；启发}{Her story has inspired millions of people around the world.}}
